{"seq":49,"slug":"combinatorial-game-theory","title":"组合博弈论","stage":"DONE","category":"mathematics-statistics","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/combinatorial-game-theory","rating":{"composite":3.96,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":5,"strategic":4},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"组合博弈论\">组合博弈论</h1><p>有两个人轮流在一堆石子里取子，谁取走最后一颗谁赢——这样一个孩童都能玩的游戏，背后却藏着一整套能给&quot;游戏本身&quot;赋予数值、能把两局棋&quot;相加&quot;、甚至能造出比任何实数都小却不为零的&quot;无穷小&quot;的数学。这就是组合博弈论（Combinatorial Game Theory，CGT）研究的世界：双人、轮流、信息完全公开、没有掷骰子的运气成分、也没有同时出手的博弈。它诞生于 Bouton 1901 年对 Nim 的完全解答，成熟于 Conway 的《论数与游戏》（ONAG）与 Berlekamp、Conway、Guy 合著的《稳操胜券》（Winning Ways）。</p>\n<p>CGT 与经济学里的经典博弈论是两门不同的学科。经典博弈论关心的是囚徒困境、纳什均衡、混合策略、不完全信息下的收益最大化；它的核心问题是&quot;理性的自利者会怎么选&quot;。CGT 则把游戏当作代数对象来研究：它不问&quot;收益是多少&quot;，而问&quot;在最优对抗下，谁必胜、还差多少手、这局棋值几分&quot;。因此本 hub 与本目录下的 <code>16_game-theory</code>（经典博弈论）是互补而非重叠的两支——前者研究可加、可比较、有值的组合游戏，后者研究均衡与激励。凡涉及纳什均衡、支付矩阵、囚徒困境的内容，本 hub 一律点到即止并链接过去。</p>\n<p>本 hub 由四条主线递进构成。第一条是<strong>基础</strong>：先讲清 CGT 为何独立成科，再给出&quot;公平游戏&quot;与&quot;党派游戏&quot;这条贯穿全书的分类，最后建立&quot;游戏即 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>∣</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mi>R</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\{G^L \\mid G^R\\}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0913em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">{</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8413em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">L</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0913em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8413em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0077em;\">R</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">}</span></span></span></span></span>&quot;的递归位置模型——这是后面一切的地基。第二条是<strong>公平游戏</strong>：所有玩家在任何位置都有相同走法的游戏。从 Nim 与异或出发，引出 Grundy 数（nimber）与 mex，最终抵达把整个公平游戏世界统一起来的 Sprague-Grundy 定理——任何公平游戏都等价于一堆 Nim。第三条是<strong>党派游戏</strong>：左右两方走法不同的游戏（围棋、Domineering、Hackenbush）。这里游戏不再只有 nimber，而是有了真正的&quot;值&quot;，甚至构造出超现实数与无穷小，并用温度理论刻画&quot;这一步有多急&quot;。第四条是<strong>应用与边界</strong>：如何用计算机求解游戏、建残局库，如何用 CGT 拆解围棋官子与各类谜题，以及这门学科在混杂游戏、misère 规则、循环游戏面前的前沿与局限。</p>\n<p>推荐的学习路径分三类读者。若你是算法竞赛或程序员，最短路径是&quot;基础第 3 篇模型 → 公平游戏全章 → 应用第 1、2 篇&quot;，因为 Nim、Grundy、Sprague-Grundy 直接对应博弈类算法题；党派游戏与超现实数可作为进阶选读。若你是数学爱好者，建议顺序通读，尤其不要跳过党派游戏与超现实数——那是 Conway 最惊艳的构造。若你是围棋或棋类玩家，可以先读基础，然后直奔第三章温度理论与应用第 2 篇的围棋官子。</p>\n<p>前置知识方面：理解公平游戏一章只需要熟悉二进制与异或运算（可参考 <code>10_number-theory</code> 的模运算）；党派游戏一章会用到少量序关系与群的直觉；温度理论涉及分数值的比较但不需要微积分。整体而言，CGT 的门槛不在于高等数学，而在于愿意接受&quot;游戏本身可以是一个数&quot;这种不寻常的抽象。读完本 hub，你会带走两样东西：一套能亲手判定谁必胜的可操作技术，以及一个被 Conway 亲手扩张过的、比实数系更辽阔的数系。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/combinatorial-game-theory/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"why-cgt","title":"为何组合博弈论","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/combinatorial-game-theory/foundations/why-cgt"},{"seq":2,"slug":"impartial-vs-partisan","title":"公平与党派游戏","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/combinatorial-game-theory/foundations/impartial-vs-partisan"},{"seq":3,"slug":"game-model","title":"游戏与位置模型","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/combinatorial-game-theory/foundations/game-model"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"impartial","title":"公平游戏","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/combinatorial-game-theory/impartial","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"nim-game","title":"Nim 与异或","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/combinatorial-game-theory/impartial/nim-game"},{"seq":2,"slug":"grundy-numbers","title":"Grundy 数 (nimber)","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/combinatorial-game-theory/impartial/grundy-numbers"},{"seq":3,"slug":"sprague-grundy","title":"Sprague-Grundy 定理","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/combinatorial-game-theory/impartial/sprague-grundy"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"partisan","title":"党派游戏","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/combinatorial-game-theory/partisan","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"game-sums","title":"游戏的和与值","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/combinatorial-game-theory/partisan/game-sums"},{"seq":2,"slug":"surreal-numbers","title":"超现实数","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/combinatorial-game-theory/partisan/surreal-numbers"},{"seq":3,"slug":"temperature-theory","title":"温度与热博弈","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/combinatorial-game-theory/partisan/temperature-theory"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"practice","title":"应用","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/combinatorial-game-theory/practice","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"solving-games","title":"求解与残局库","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/combinatorial-game-theory/practice/solving-games"},{"seq":2,"slug":"game-applications","title":"应用（围棋残局/谜题）","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/combinatorial-game-theory/practice/game-applications"},{"seq":3,"slug":"cgt-in-practice","title":"前沿与边界","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/combinatorial-game-theory/practice/cgt-in-practice"}]}]}